'' =================================================================================================
''
''   File....... RT_power_loss_tests.spin2
''   Purpose.... This object builds, straight on the flash, the block states a power cut can leave: a
''               duplicate ID, an orphan body block, a head block that was programmed and never
''               activated, and a block whose CRC no longer matches.  For each it checks that
''               can_mount() reports it without changing any block, that mount() repairs it with the
''               right status, that the files which should survive read back whole, and that a second
''               mount is clean.  It also checks that a block move during create_file() leaves the
''               new file whole across a mount
''   Author..... Stephen M Moraco
''               -- see below for terms of use
''   E-mail.....stephen@ironsheep.biz
''   Started.... NOV 2026
''   Updated.... 24 NOV 2026
''
'' =================================================================================================

{ Each group starts from a fresh format with three files: an untouched two-block file, a two-block
  target file whose blocks the group copies, and a one-block file.  The filesystem is then unmounted
  and the state is built with the driver's block hooks, which change the flash and nothing else.
  Every block built is read back before can_mount() or mount() is called, so a case cannot pass
  when its state was not built.  can_mount() must change no block: every block the group touched is
  fingerprinted before and after it.

  How the driver treats each state, from the three mount passes:
  - a block whose lifecycle is not active (inactive or cancelled) is skipped at once by mount() and
    can_mount(), whatever else it holds: it is never checked, used, cancelled or reported;
  - an active block whose CRC does not match is cancelled by mount(), which reports
    E_BAD_BLOCKS_REMOVED, and can_mount() is FALSE;
  - two active blocks with one ID: mount() keeps the newer lifecycle and cancels the older one,
    returning SUCCESS; can_mount() is FALSE because mount() changes a block;
  - an active block that no file chain reaches (an orphan, or a block of a broken chain) is cancelled
    by mount(), which reports E_BAD_BLOCKS_REMOVED, and can_mount() is FALSE.

  So a stop at any step of a file operation leaves one of these states:
  - after an erase, or after any page of a block program: the block is inactive and is ignored;
  - after a body block is activated while its commit chain head is still inactive (write_block(),
    create_file()): the bodies already activated are orphans;
  - after the activate of a replacement, before the old copy is cancelled (rewrite_block(), rename(),
    a block move, a close() or flush() that replaces a head or the last block, a circular trim): a
    duplicate ID, plus orphans where the old copy led to blocks the new one does not;
  - after a cancel in a chain delete or a format: the blocks not yet cancelled that no chain reaches
    are orphans;
  - after the last step of an operation: nothing to repair.

  create_file() writes its head block first and activates it only after the last block, and every block
  it takes for a body block can be a block move.  A move copies an active block with the next lifecycle and
  activates the copy, so a move of the still-inactive head would keep a copy whose CRC is not the one the
  head's activation needs, and the next mount would cancel the file.  The block-move group names one free
  block for the allocations: the head block is written there, and the next allocation picks it again.  The
  file must then mount, read back whole, and leave can_mount() TRUE.

  The hook refusal cases run last: a hook that did not check its address would write the flash below
  the filesystem.  They use the activate operation with the inactive lifecycle, which writes a byte of
  all ones, so a refused call that did reach the flash would still clear no bit.
}

CON

     _CLKFREQ        = 320_000_000

{
    ' debug via serial to RPi (using RPi gateway pins)
    '  USES LED1 (56) and LED2 (57) pins
    DEBUG_PIN_TX = 57           ' GRY GPIO 10
    DEBUG_PIN_RX = 56           ' WHT GPIO 8 (gnd is BLK GPIO 6)
    DEBUG_WINDOWS_OFF = -1      ' no debug windows showing
    DEBUG_BAUD = 2_000_000      ' comms at 2Mbit
'}

OBJ
    flash : "flash_fs"
    utils : "RT_utilities"

CON ' ---- Test Geometry ----

    BODY_TAIL_BYTES = 1000                              ' bytes of a two-block file that go into its body block
    FILE_BYTES = flash.BYTES_IN_HEAD_BLOCK + BODY_TAIL_BYTES ' bytes of each two-block file: a full head block and part of a body
    ONE_BLOCK_BYTES = 100                               ' bytes of the one-block file
    FILE_COUNT = 3                                      ' files each group writes
    KEEP_SEED = 1                                       ' first data byte of the untouched file
    TARGET_SEED = 2                                     ' first data byte of the target file
    CRC_SEED = 3                                        ' first data byte of the one-block file
    BYTE_MASK = $FF                                     ' keeps a value to one byte
    MAX_TOUCHED = 4                                     ' blocks one group touches at most
    HEAD_COPY_TOUCH_IDX = 1                             ' entry of the inactive head copy among the blocks its group touches
    NO_BLOCK = -1                                       ' a block address no block has
    FIRST_BLOCK_ADDR = 0                                ' first block address of the filesystem
    BEFORE_FIRST_BLOCK = -1                             ' the block address just below the filesystem
    ORPHAN_ID = flash.BLOCKS - 1                        ' a block ID no block of the three files has
    NOT_A_BLOCK_OP = 0                                  ' an operation the block hook does not have
    NO_SOURCE = 0                                       ' block image address of a hook operation that programs no image
    NO_CYCLE = 0                                        ' lifecycle of a hook operation that writes no lifecycle
    MOVED_FILE_BYTES = flash.BYTES_IN_HEAD_BLOCK + flash.BYTES_IN_BODY_BLOCK + BODY_TAIL_BYTES ' bytes of the file made with create_file(): three blocks
    MOVED_FILL = $6C                                    ' fill value of the file made with create_file()

CON ' ---- Block Format ----

    ' The first long of a block, and the CRC at its end:
    '  NEXT_TOP..NEXT_BOTTOM   - NextID of a block with more blocks after it, EndPtr of a last block
    '  ID_TOP..ID_BOTTOM       - the block's own ID
    '  CYCLE_TOP..CYCLE_BOTTOM - the lifecycle, in the first byte
    '  BODY_BIT                - 1 in a body block, 0 in a head block
    '  CRC_BYTES               - bytes of the CRC long at the end of the block, which covers the bytes before it
    NEXT_TOP = 31
    NEXT_BOTTOM = 20
    ID_TOP = 19
    ID_BOTTOM = 8
    CYCLE_TOP = 7
    CYCLE_BOTTOM = 5
    BODY_BIT = 1
    CRC_BYTES = 4
    FIRST_DATA_BYTE = 1                                 ' first byte after the byte that holds the lifecycle
    BLOCK_CRC_POLY = $AD0424F3 rev 31                   ' polynomial of the block CRC

    ' Lifecycles: an active block has one zero bit, the three active values follow each other in the
    ' order CYCLE_FIRST, CYCLE_SECOND, CYCLE_THIRD, CYCLE_FIRST, and the later one of a pair is the newer;
    ' an inactive block has no zero bit; a cancelled block has two or three
    CYCLE_FIRST = %011
    CYCLE_SECOND = %101
    CYCLE_THIRD = %110
    CYCLE_INACTIVE = %111
    ACTIVE_ONES = 2                                     ' one bits of an active lifecycle
    CANCELLED_MAX_ONES = 1                              ' most one bits of a cancelled lifecycle

DAT ' ---- Files ----

keepFile        BYTE    "pl_keep.bin", 0                ' a two-block file no case touches
targetFile      BYTE    "pl_target.bin", 0              ' a two-block file whose blocks the cases copy
crcFile         BYTE    "pl_crc.bin", 0                 ' a one-block file whose block one case corrupts
movedFile       BYTE    "pl_moved.bin", 0               ' a three-block file made with create_file() while a block is named

DAT ' ---- Block Addresses and State ----

bSetUp          LONG    FALSE                           ' TRUE when the group's files were written and their blocks found
targetHeadAddr  LONG    0                               ' head block of the target file
targetBodyAddr  LONG    0                               ' body block of the target file
crcHeadAddr     LONG    0                               ' the one block of the one-block file
targetHeadId    LONG    0                               ' block ID of the target file's head block
targetBodyId    LONG    0                               ' block ID of the target file's body block
copyAddr        LONG    0                               ' block a case programmed
secondCopyAddr  LONG    0                               ' second block a case programmed
copyCycle       LONG    0                               ' lifecycle the copy was given
touchedCount    LONG    0                               ' blocks in touchedAddr
touchedAddr     LONG    0[MAX_TOUCHED]                  ' blocks the group touched or copied
printsBefore    LONG    0[MAX_TOUCHED]                  ' fingerprint of each touched block before can_mount()
printsAfter     LONG    0[MAX_TOUCHED]                  ' fingerprint of each touched block after can_mount()

DAT ' ---- Buffers ----

dataBuf         BYTE    0[FILE_BYTES]                   ' what a file is written from and read into
sourceBuf       BYTE    0[flash.BLOCK_SIZE]             ' the block a case copies, as read before the copy
copyBuf         BYTE    0[flash.BLOCK_SIZE]             ' the image a case programs


PUB go() | status, pFailedCall
'' Run every power-loss state test, then show the result.
''

' Local Variables:
' @local status - status of the format and mount that start the run
' @local pFailedCall - address of the name of the call that failed

    pFailedCall := @"format()"
    status := flash.format()      ' Comment out this line to not erase all files
    if status == flash.SUCCESS
        pFailedCall := @"mount()"
        status := flash.mount()

    if status == flash.SUCCESS
        utils.checkDriverInstance(flash.MAX_FILES_OPEN)

        utils.showChipAndDriverVersion()
        utils.setCheckCountPerTest(1)                   ' each check of a case is shown on its own

        testDuplicateId()
        testOrphanBody()
        testInactiveHead()
        testBadCrcBlock()
        testMovedNewHead()
        debug("* The next calls give the block hooks addresses outside the filesystem")
        testHookRefusals()
    else
        utils.showError(pFailedCall, status)
        utils.startTest(@"format() and mount()")        ' a filesystem that did not mount is a failed run
        utils.evaluateResultNegError(status, flash.SUCCESS)

    debug("* Test Complete")
    utils.ShowTestResult(@"RT_power_loss_tests")


PRI testDuplicateId()
' A copy of the target file's body block with the next lifecycle: can_mount() is FALSE, mount() keeps the newer copy, cancels the older one and returns SUCCESS.

    utils.startTestGroup(@"a duplicate ID: a copy of a body block with the next lifecycle")
    setUpFiles()
    buildDuplicate()
    canMountStep(@"can_mount() is FALSE for a duplicate ID and changes no block", FALSE)
    mountDuplicate()
    survivorsStep(TRUE)
    secondMountStep()


PRI buildDuplicate() | pBlock, status, actStatus
' Copy the target file's body block to a free block with the next lifecycle, activate it and read it back, as one test.

' Local Variables:
' @local pBlock - address of a block read back
' @local status - what the program operation returned
' @local actStatus - what the activate operation returned

    utils.startTest(@"copy the body block of the target file, activate the copy with the next lifecycle and read it back")
    utils.evaluateSubValue(bSetUp, @"the files were set up", TRUE)
    if bSetUp
        readInto(targetBodyAddr, @sourceBuf)
        copyCycle := nextCycle(cycleOf(@sourceBuf))
        copyAddr := findFreeBlock(NO_BLOCK)
        bytemove(@copyBuf, @sourceBuf, flash.BLOCK_SIZE)
        status := flash.TEST_changeBlock(flash.TEST_BLK_PROGRAM, copyAddr, @copyBuf, copyCycle)
        actStatus := flash.TEST_changeBlock(flash.TEST_BLK_ACTIVATE, copyAddr, NO_SOURCE, copyCycle)
        debug("  body block ", uhex_word_(targetBodyAddr), " copied to block ", uhex_word_(copyAddr))
        utils.evaluateSubStatus(status, @"program the copy", flash.SUCCESS)
        utils.evaluateSubStatus(actStatus, @"activate the copy", flash.SUCCESS)

        pBlock := readInto(copyAddr, @copyBuf)
        utils.evaluateSubValue(pBlock > 0, @"the copy was read back", TRUE)
        utils.evaluateSubValue(cycleOf(@copyBuf), @"lifecycle of the copy is the next one", copyCycle)
        utils.evaluateSubValue(idOf(@copyBuf), @"block ID of the copy is the body block's", targetBodyId)
        utils.evaluateSubValue(isCrcGood(@copyBuf), @"the copy's CRC matches", TRUE)
        utils.evaluateSubValue(dataMatches(@copyBuf, @sourceBuf), @"the copy holds the body block's data", TRUE)

        readInto(targetBodyAddr, @copyBuf)
        utils.evaluateSubValue(cycleOf(@copyBuf), @"the body block keeps its lifecycle", cycleOf(@sourceBuf))
        utils.evaluateSubValue(isActive(cycleOf(@sourceBuf)), @"the body block is active", TRUE)

        setTouched(targetBodyAddr, copyAddr, NO_BLOCK, NO_BLOCK)


PRI mountDuplicate()
' mount() resolves the duplicate silently: SUCCESS, the older copy cancelled and the newer one kept, as one test.

    utils.startTest(@"mount() cancels the older copy, keeps the newer one and returns SUCCESS")
    utils.evaluateSubValue(bSetUp, @"the files were set up", TRUE)
    if bSetUp
        mountAndCheck(flash.SUCCESS)                    ' a duplicate ID is repaired without a status
        readInto(targetBodyAddr, @copyBuf)
        utils.evaluateSubValue(isCancelled(cycleOf(@copyBuf)), @"the older copy is cancelled", TRUE)
        readInto(copyAddr, @copyBuf)
        utils.evaluateSubValue(cycleOf(@copyBuf), @"the newer copy keeps its lifecycle", copyCycle)


PRI testOrphanBody()
' A copy of the target file's body block under an ID no file uses: can_mount() is FALSE, mount() cancels it and returns E_BAD_BLOCKS_REMOVED.

    utils.startTestGroup(@"an orphan body block: an active body block no file reaches")
    setUpFiles()
    buildOrphan()
    canMountStep(@"can_mount() is FALSE for an orphan body block and changes no block", FALSE)
    mountOrphan()
    survivorsStep(TRUE)
    secondMountStep()


PRI buildOrphan() | pBlock, status, actStatus
' Copy the target file's body block to a free block under an unused ID, activate it and read it back, as one test.

' Local Variables:
' @local pBlock - address of a block read back
' @local status - what the program operation returned
' @local actStatus - what the activate operation returned

    utils.startTest(@"copy the body block of the target file under an unused ID, activate it and read it back")
    utils.evaluateSubValue(bSetUp, @"the files were set up", TRUE)
    if bSetUp
        readInto(targetBodyAddr, @sourceBuf)
        copyCycle := CYCLE_FIRST                        ' the lifecycle a new body block is given
        copyAddr := findFreeBlock(NO_BLOCK)
        bytemove(@copyBuf, @sourceBuf, flash.BLOCK_SIZE)
        LONG[@copyBuf].[ID_TOP..ID_BOTTOM] := ORPHAN_ID
        status := flash.TEST_changeBlock(flash.TEST_BLK_PROGRAM, copyAddr, @copyBuf, copyCycle)
        actStatus := flash.TEST_changeBlock(flash.TEST_BLK_ACTIVATE, copyAddr, NO_SOURCE, copyCycle)
        debug("  orphan body block at block ", uhex_word_(copyAddr))
        utils.evaluateSubStatus(status, @"program the orphan", flash.SUCCESS)
        utils.evaluateSubStatus(actStatus, @"activate the orphan", flash.SUCCESS)

        pBlock := readInto(copyAddr, @copyBuf)
        utils.evaluateSubValue(pBlock > 0, @"the orphan was read back", TRUE)
        utils.evaluateSubValue(cycleOf(@copyBuf), @"lifecycle of the orphan", copyCycle)
        utils.evaluateSubValue(idOf(@copyBuf), @"block ID of the orphan", ORPHAN_ID)
        utils.evaluateSubValue(LONG[@copyBuf].[BODY_BIT], @"the orphan is a body block", 1)
        utils.evaluateSubValue(isCrcGood(@copyBuf), @"the orphan's CRC matches", TRUE)

        setTouched(copyAddr, targetBodyAddr, NO_BLOCK, NO_BLOCK)


PRI mountOrphan()
' mount() cancels the orphan and reports it, as one test.

    utils.startTest(@"mount() cancels the orphan body block and returns E_BAD_BLOCKS_REMOVED")
    utils.evaluateSubValue(bSetUp, @"the files were set up", TRUE)
    if bSetUp
        mountAndCheck(flash.E_BAD_BLOCKS_REMOVED)       ' an active block no file reaches is cancelled and reported
        readInto(copyAddr, @copyBuf)
        utils.evaluateSubValue(isCancelled(cycleOf(@copyBuf)), @"the orphan is cancelled", TRUE)


PRI testInactiveHead()
' A copy of the target file's head block with the next lifecycle, programmed and never activated, leading to an active body block: the head copy is ignored, the body copy is an orphan.

    utils.startTestGroup(@"a head block programmed and never activated, with the body block it leads to")
    setUpFiles()
    buildInactiveHead()
    canMountStep(@"can_mount() is TRUE while the one change is a head block that was never activated, and changes no block", TRUE)
    buildInactiveHeadBody()
    canMountStep(@"can_mount() is FALSE once the body block the inactive head leads to is active, and changes no block", FALSE)
    mountInactiveHead()
    survivorsStep(TRUE)
    secondMountStep()


PRI buildInactiveHead() | pBlock, status
' Copy the target file's head block to a free block with the next lifecycle and a NextID no block has, program it without activating it and read it back, as one test.

' Local Variables:
' @local pBlock - address of a block read back
' @local status - what the program operation returned

    utils.startTest(@"copy the head block of the target file with the next lifecycle, never activate it, and read it back")
    utils.evaluateSubValue(bSetUp, @"the files were set up", TRUE)
    if bSetUp
        readInto(targetHeadAddr, @sourceBuf)
        copyCycle := nextCycle(cycleOf(@sourceBuf))
        copyAddr := findFreeBlock(NO_BLOCK)
        bytemove(@copyBuf, @sourceBuf, flash.BLOCK_SIZE)
        LONG[@copyBuf].[NEXT_TOP..NEXT_BOTTOM] := ORPHAN_ID
        status := flash.TEST_changeBlock(flash.TEST_BLK_PROGRAM, copyAddr, @copyBuf, copyCycle)
        debug("  inactive head block at block ", uhex_word_(copyAddr))
        utils.evaluateSubStatus(status, @"program the head copy", flash.SUCCESS)

        pBlock := readInto(copyAddr, @copyBuf)
        utils.evaluateSubValue(pBlock > 0, @"the head copy was read back", TRUE)
        utils.evaluateSubValue(cycleOf(@copyBuf), @"the head copy is inactive", CYCLE_INACTIVE)
        utils.evaluateSubValue(idOf(@copyBuf), @"block ID of the head copy is the head block's", targetHeadId)
        utils.evaluateSubValue(LONG[@copyBuf].[NEXT_TOP..NEXT_BOTTOM], @"NextID of the head copy", ORPHAN_ID)
        BYTE[@copyBuf].[CYCLE_TOP..CYCLE_BOTTOM] := copyCycle
        utils.evaluateSubValue(isCrcGood(@copyBuf), @"the head copy's CRC matches once activated with the next lifecycle", TRUE)

        setTouched(targetHeadAddr, copyAddr, NO_BLOCK, NO_BLOCK)


PRI buildInactiveHeadBody() | pBlock, status, actStatus
' Copy the target file's body block, with the ID the inactive head leads to and one data byte changed, to a free block, activate it and read it back, as one test.

' Local Variables:
' @local pBlock - address of a block read back
' @local status - what the program operation returned
' @local actStatus - what the activate operation returned

    utils.startTest(@"copy the body block under the ID the inactive head leads to, with one data byte changed, activate it and read it back")
    utils.evaluateSubValue(bSetUp, @"the files were set up", TRUE)
    if bSetUp
        readInto(targetBodyAddr, @sourceBuf)
        secondCopyAddr := findFreeBlock(copyAddr)
        bytemove(@copyBuf, @sourceBuf, flash.BLOCK_SIZE)
        LONG[@copyBuf].[ID_TOP..ID_BOTTOM] := ORPHAN_ID
        BYTE[@copyBuf][flash.ADDR_BODY_DATA] ^= BYTE_MASK  ' a file that read this block would read a byte the file never held
        status := flash.TEST_changeBlock(flash.TEST_BLK_PROGRAM, secondCopyAddr, @copyBuf, CYCLE_FIRST)
        actStatus := flash.TEST_changeBlock(flash.TEST_BLK_ACTIVATE, secondCopyAddr, NO_SOURCE, CYCLE_FIRST)
        debug("  body block the inactive head leads to at block ", uhex_word_(secondCopyAddr))
        utils.evaluateSubStatus(status, @"program the body copy", flash.SUCCESS)
        utils.evaluateSubStatus(actStatus, @"activate the body copy", flash.SUCCESS)

        pBlock := readInto(secondCopyAddr, @copyBuf)
        utils.evaluateSubValue(pBlock > 0, @"the body copy was read back", TRUE)
        utils.evaluateSubValue(cycleOf(@copyBuf), @"lifecycle of the body copy", CYCLE_FIRST)
        utils.evaluateSubValue(idOf(@copyBuf), @"block ID of the body copy", ORPHAN_ID)
        utils.evaluateSubValue(isCrcGood(@copyBuf), @"the body copy's CRC matches", TRUE)
        utils.evaluateSubValue(BYTE[@copyBuf][flash.ADDR_BODY_DATA] == BYTE[@sourceBuf][flash.ADDR_BODY_DATA], @"the body copy's first data byte differs from the body block's", FALSE)

        setTouched(targetHeadAddr, copyAddr, targetBodyAddr, secondCopyAddr)


PRI mountInactiveHead() | printNow
' mount() cancels the active body copy, reports it, and leaves the inactive head copy as it was, as one test.

' Local Variables:
' @local printNow - fingerprint of the inactive head copy after mount()

    utils.startTest(@"mount() cancels the body copy, returns E_BAD_BLOCKS_REMOVED and leaves the inactive head copy as it was")
    utils.evaluateSubValue(bSetUp, @"the files were set up", TRUE)
    if bSetUp
        mountAndCheck(flash.E_BAD_BLOCKS_REMOVED)       ' the active body copy is reached by no active head
        readInto(secondCopyAddr, @copyBuf)
        utils.evaluateSubValue(isCancelled(cycleOf(@copyBuf)), @"the body copy is cancelled", TRUE)
        readInto(copyAddr, @copyBuf)
        utils.evaluateSubValue(cycleOf(@copyBuf), @"the head copy is still inactive", CYCLE_INACTIVE)
        printNow := blockPrint(copyAddr)
        utils.evaluateSubValue(printNow, @"the head copy is unchanged by mount()", printsAfter[HEAD_COPY_TOUCH_IDX])


PRI testBadCrcBlock()
' The one-block file's block with a reserved bit cleared, so its CRC no longer matches: can_mount() is FALSE, mount() cancels it and returns E_BAD_BLOCKS_REMOVED.

    utils.startTestGroup(@"an active block whose CRC no longer matches")
    setUpFiles()
    buildBadCrc()
    canMountStep(@"can_mount() is FALSE for a block whose CRC does not match and changes no block", FALSE)
    mountBadCrc()
    survivorsStep(FALSE)
    secondMountStep()


PRI buildBadCrc() | pBlock, status
' Clear the reserved bit of the one-block file's block and read the block back, as one test.

' Local Variables:
' @local pBlock - address of a block read back
' @local status - what the corrupt operation returned

    utils.startTest(@"clear a reserved bit of the one-block file's block and read it back")
    utils.evaluateSubValue(bSetUp, @"the files were set up", TRUE)
    if bSetUp
        readInto(crcHeadAddr, @sourceBuf)
        utils.evaluateSubValue(BYTE[@sourceBuf] & flash.TEST_CORRUPT_BIT, @"the reserved bit is set before the change", flash.TEST_CORRUPT_BIT)
        utils.evaluateSubValue(isCrcGood(@sourceBuf), @"the block's CRC matches before the change", TRUE)
        status := flash.TEST_changeBlock(flash.TEST_BLK_CORRUPT, crcHeadAddr, NO_SOURCE, NO_CYCLE)
        debug("  block ", uhex_word_(crcHeadAddr), " corrupted")
        utils.evaluateSubStatus(status, @"clear the reserved bit", flash.SUCCESS)

        pBlock := readInto(crcHeadAddr, @copyBuf)
        utils.evaluateSubValue(pBlock > 0, @"the block was read back", TRUE)
        utils.evaluateSubValue(BYTE[@copyBuf], @"first byte of the block lost the reserved bit", BYTE[@sourceBuf] & !flash.TEST_CORRUPT_BIT & BYTE_MASK)
        utils.evaluateSubValue(cycleOf(@copyBuf), @"the block keeps its lifecycle", cycleOf(@sourceBuf))
        utils.evaluateSubValue(isActive(cycleOf(@copyBuf)), @"the block is active", TRUE)
        utils.evaluateSubValue(isCrcGood(@copyBuf), @"the block's CRC matches after the change", FALSE)

        setTouched(crcHeadAddr, NO_BLOCK, NO_BLOCK, NO_BLOCK)


PRI mountBadCrc()
' mount() cancels the block whose CRC does not match and reports it, as one test.

    utils.startTest(@"mount() cancels the block whose CRC does not match and returns E_BAD_BLOCKS_REMOVED")
    utils.evaluateSubValue(bSetUp, @"the files were set up", TRUE)
    if bSetUp
        mountAndCheck(flash.E_BAD_BLOCKS_REMOVED)       ' a block cancelled for its CRC is a bad block removed
        readInto(crcHeadAddr, @copyBuf)
        utils.evaluateSubValue(isCancelled(cycleOf(@copyBuf)), @"the block is cancelled", TRUE)


PRI testMovedNewHead()
' create_file() with one free block named for the allocations: its head block is written there and picked again while still inactive; the file must survive a mount whole.

    utils.startTestGroup(@"a block move during create_file() and the new file's inactive head block")
    createWithNamedBlock()
    movedHeadMountStep()


PRI createWithNamedBlock() | status, namedAddr, setStatus, clearStatus, headAddr
' Format, name a free block for the allocations, make a three-block file with create_file() and clear the name, as one test; bSetUp tells the next step whether it worked.

' Local Variables:
' @local status - what format() and create_file() returned
' @local namedAddr - the free block named for the allocations
' @local setStatus - what naming the block returned
' @local clearStatus - what clearing the name returned
' @local headAddr - the block that holds the new file's head block after create_file()

    utils.startTest(@"create_file() of a three-block file while the block allocations are named to take one free block")
    bSetUp := FALSE
    status := flash.format()
    utils.evaluateSubStatus(status, @"format()", flash.SUCCESS)
    namedAddr := findFreeBlock(NO_BLOCK)
    utils.evaluateSubValue(flash.TEST_blockStateOf(namedAddr), @"the named block is free", flash.B_FREE)

    setStatus := flash.TEST_setTargetBlock(namedAddr)
    ' the head block is written to the free named block, and each body block's allocation picks the named block again
    status := flash.create_file(@movedFile, MOVED_FILL, MOVED_FILE_BYTES)
    clearStatus := flash.TEST_setTargetBlock(flash.NOT_ENABLED)
    _, _, headAddr, _ := flash.TEST_get4kBlockAndNextAtOffset(@movedFile, 0)
    debug("  named block ", uhex_word_(namedAddr), ", the new file's head block is at block ", uhex_word_(headAddr))

    utils.evaluateSubStatus(setStatus, @"name the block", flash.SUCCESS)
    utils.evaluateSubStatus(status, @"create_file()", flash.SUCCESS)
    utils.evaluateSubStatus(clearStatus, @"clear the name", flash.SUCCESS)
    utils.evaluateSubValue(flash.TEST_blockStateOf(namedAddr) <> flash.B_FREE, @"the named block holds a block of the new file", TRUE)
    bSetUp := status == flash.SUCCESS and setStatus == flash.SUCCESS and clearStatus == flash.SUCCESS


PRI movedHeadMountStep() | status
' Unmount, then check can_mount() is TRUE, mount() returns SUCCESS and the new file reads back whole, as one test.

' Local Variables:
' @local status - what unmount() returned

    utils.startTest(@"the file made while a block was named survives an unmount and a mount, and reads back whole")
    utils.evaluateSubValue(bSetUp, @"the file was made", TRUE)
    if bSetUp
        status := flash.unmount()
        utils.evaluateSubStatus(status, @"unmount()", flash.SUCCESS)
        utils.evaluateSubValue(flash.can_mount(), @"can_mount()", TRUE)
        mountAndCheck(flash.SUCCESS)                    ' a head block whose CRC matches its active lifecycle keeps the whole file
        utils.evaluateSubValue(flash.exists(@movedFile), @"the file exists", TRUE)
        utils.evaluateSubValue(fillMatches(@movedFile, MOVED_FILE_BYTES, MOVED_FILL), @"the file reads back whole", TRUE)


PRI testHookRefusals()
' The block hooks refuse the block addresses just outside the filesystem and an operation they do not have, and accept the addresses inside it.

    utils.startTestGroup(@"the block hooks refuse an address outside the filesystem")
    refuseChange()
    refuseRead()
    acceptInside()


PRI refuseChange()
' TEST_changeBlock() refuses -1, BLOCKS and an operation it does not have, as one test.

    utils.startTest(@"TEST_changeBlock() refuses block addresses -1 and BLOCKS and an operation it does not have")
    ' each call below is refused before any flash command is sent
    checkStatus(flash.TEST_changeBlock(flash.TEST_BLK_ACTIVATE, BEFORE_FIRST_BLOCK, NO_SOURCE, CYCLE_INACTIVE), flash.E_TEST_BAD_BLOCK_ARG)
    checkStatus(flash.TEST_changeBlock(flash.TEST_BLK_ACTIVATE, flash.BLOCKS, NO_SOURCE, CYCLE_INACTIVE), flash.E_TEST_BAD_BLOCK_ARG)
    checkStatus(flash.TEST_changeBlock(NOT_A_BLOCK_OP, FIRST_BLOCK_ADDR, NO_SOURCE, CYCLE_INACTIVE), flash.E_TEST_BAD_BLOCK_ARG)


PRI refuseRead()
' TEST_readBlock() refuses -1 and BLOCKS, as one test.

    utils.startTest(@"TEST_readBlock() refuses block addresses -1 and BLOCKS")
    ' a refused read returns the error code instead of a buffer address
    checkStatus(flash.TEST_readBlock(BEFORE_FIRST_BLOCK), flash.E_TEST_BAD_BLOCK_ARG)
    checkStatus(flash.TEST_readBlock(flash.BLOCKS), flash.E_TEST_BAD_BLOCK_ARG)


PRI acceptInside() | freeAddr, printBefore, printNow, status, errCode
' The hooks accept the first and last block addresses, and an activate with the inactive lifecycle leaves a free block as it was, as one test.

' Local Variables:
' @local freeAddr - a block no file uses
' @local printBefore - fingerprint of that block before the activate
' @local printNow - fingerprint of that block after it
' @local status - what the activate returned
' @local errCode - error() after the activate

    utils.startTest(@"the block hooks accept block addresses 0 and BLOCKS - 1")
    utils.evaluateSubValue(flash.TEST_readBlock(FIRST_BLOCK_ADDR) > 0, @"TEST_readBlock(0) returns a buffer", TRUE)
    utils.evaluateSubStatus(flash.error(), @"error() after TEST_readBlock(0)", flash.SUCCESS)
    utils.evaluateSubValue(flash.TEST_readBlock(flash.BLOCKS - 1) > 0, @"TEST_readBlock(BLOCKS - 1) returns a buffer", TRUE)
    utils.evaluateSubStatus(flash.error(), @"error() after TEST_readBlock(BLOCKS - 1)", flash.SUCCESS)

    freeAddr := findFreeBlock(NO_BLOCK)
    printBefore := blockPrint(freeAddr)
    status := flash.TEST_changeBlock(flash.TEST_BLK_ACTIVATE, freeAddr, NO_SOURCE, CYCLE_INACTIVE)
    errCode := flash.error()
    printNow := blockPrint(freeAddr)
    utils.evaluateSubStatus(status, @"activate a free block with the inactive lifecycle", flash.SUCCESS)
    utils.evaluateSubStatus(errCode, @"error() after the activate", flash.SUCCESS)
    utils.evaluateSubValue(printNow, @"the free block is unchanged", printBefore)


PRI setUpFiles() | status, pBuff, pBuff2, bKeep, bTarget, bCrc, bIdsFree
' Format, write the three files, find their blocks and unmount, as one test; bSetUp tells the later steps whether it worked.

' Local Variables:
' @local status - what format() and unmount() returned
' @local pBuff - head block buffer the block hook returned
' @local pBuff2 - body block buffer the block hook returned
' @local bKeep - TRUE when the untouched file was written and has a head and a body block
' @local bTarget - TRUE when the target file was written and has a head and a body block
' @local bCrc - TRUE when the one-block file was written and has one block
' @local bIdsFree - TRUE when no block of the three files uses the orphan ID

    utils.startTest(@"set up: format, write three files, find their blocks and unmount")
    bSetUp := FALSE
    bIdsFree := TRUE
    status := flash.format()
    utils.evaluateSubStatus(status, @"format()", flash.SUCCESS)
    bSetUp := status == flash.SUCCESS

    bKeep := writeFile(@keepFile, FILE_BYTES, KEEP_SEED)
    pBuff, pBuff2, _, _ := flash.TEST_get4kBlockAndNextAtOffset(@keepFile, 0)
    bKeep := bKeep and pBuff <> 0 and pBuff2 <> 0
    if bKeep
        bIdsFree := bIdsFree and idOf(pBuff) <> ORPHAN_ID and idOf(pBuff2) <> ORPHAN_ID
    utils.evaluateSubValue(bKeep, @"the untouched file is written with a head and a body block", TRUE)

    bTarget := writeFile(@targetFile, FILE_BYTES, TARGET_SEED)
    pBuff, pBuff2, targetHeadAddr, targetBodyAddr := flash.TEST_get4kBlockAndNextAtOffset(@targetFile, 0)
    bTarget := bTarget and pBuff <> 0 and pBuff2 <> 0
    if bTarget
        targetHeadId := idOf(pBuff)
        targetBodyId := idOf(pBuff2)
        bIdsFree := bIdsFree and targetHeadId <> ORPHAN_ID and targetBodyId <> ORPHAN_ID
    utils.evaluateSubValue(bTarget, @"the target file is written with a head and a body block", TRUE)

    bCrc := writeFile(@crcFile, ONE_BLOCK_BYTES, CRC_SEED)
    pBuff, pBuff2, crcHeadAddr, _ := flash.TEST_get4kBlockAndNextAtOffset(@crcFile, 0)
    bCrc := bCrc and pBuff <> 0 and pBuff2 == 0
    if bCrc
        bIdsFree := bIdsFree and idOf(pBuff) <> ORPHAN_ID
    utils.evaluateSubValue(bCrc, @"the one-block file is written with one block", TRUE)
    utils.evaluateSubValue(bIdsFree, @"no block of the three files uses the orphan ID", TRUE)

    status := flash.unmount()
    utils.evaluateSubStatus(status, @"unmount()", flash.SUCCESS)
    bSetUp := bSetUp and bKeep and bTarget and bCrc and bIdsFree and status == flash.SUCCESS
    touchedCount := 0


PRI canMountStep(pTitle, bExpected) | bCanMount, touchIdx
' Call can_mount() with the filesystem unmounted, and check its answer and that every touched block is unchanged, as one test.

' @param pTitle - address of zstring naming the test
' @param bExpected - the answer can_mount() must give

' Local Variables:
' @local bCanMount - what can_mount() returned
' @local touchIdx - number of the touched block being compared

    utils.startTest(pTitle)
    utils.evaluateSubValue(bSetUp, @"the files were set up", TRUE)
    if bSetUp
        recordPrints(@printsBefore)
        bCanMount := flash.can_mount()
        recordPrints(@printsAfter)
        utils.evaluateSubValue(bCanMount, @"can_mount()", bExpected)
        utils.evaluateSubValue(flash.mounted(), @"the filesystem is still not mounted", FALSE)
        repeat touchedCount with touchIdx
            utils.evaluateSubValue(printsAfter[touchIdx], @"a touched block is unchanged by can_mount()", printsBefore[touchIdx])


PRI survivorsStep(bOneBlockFileKept) | fileCount
' Check the files that must survive read back whole, and the file count, as one test.

' @param bOneBlockFileKept - TRUE when the one-block file must survive, FALSE when mount() removed it

' Local Variables:
' @local fileCount - files the filesystem reports

    utils.startTest(@"the files that must survive read back whole")
    utils.evaluateSubValue(bSetUp, @"the files were set up", TRUE)
    if bSetUp
        utils.evaluateSubValue(fileMatches(@keepFile, FILE_BYTES, KEEP_SEED), @"the untouched file reads back whole", TRUE)
        utils.evaluateSubValue(fileMatches(@targetFile, FILE_BYTES, TARGET_SEED), @"the target file reads back whole", TRUE)
        _, _, fileCount := flash.stats()
        if bOneBlockFileKept
            utils.evaluateSubValue(fileMatches(@crcFile, ONE_BLOCK_BYTES, CRC_SEED), @"the one-block file reads back whole", TRUE)
            utils.evaluateSubValue(fileCount, @"files in the filesystem", FILE_COUNT)
        else
            utils.evaluateSubValue(flash.exists(@crcFile), @"the one-block file is gone", FALSE)
            utils.evaluateSubValue(fileCount, @"files in the filesystem", FILE_COUNT - 1)


PRI secondMountStep() | status
' Unmount, then check can_mount() is TRUE and mount() returns SUCCESS, as one test.

' Local Variables:
' @local status - what unmount() returned

    utils.startTest(@"a second mount is clean: can_mount() TRUE, then mount() SUCCESS")
    utils.evaluateSubValue(bSetUp, @"the files were set up", TRUE)
    if bSetUp
        status := flash.unmount()
        utils.evaluateSubStatus(status, @"unmount()", flash.SUCCESS)
        utils.evaluateSubValue(flash.can_mount(), @"can_mount()", TRUE)
        mountAndCheck(flash.SUCCESS)


PRI mountAndCheck(expectedStatus) | status, errCode
' Call mount() and check its status and the error() it leaves.

' @param expectedStatus - the status mount() must return and leave in error()

' Local Variables:
' @local status - what mount() returned
' @local errCode - error() after mount()

    status := flash.mount()
    errCode := flash.error()
    utils.evaluateSubStatus(status, @"mount()", expectedStatus)
    utils.evaluateSubStatus(errCode, @"error() after mount()", expectedStatus)


PRI checkStatus(returned, expectedCode) | errCode
' Check the status a call returned and the error() it left are both a code.

' @param returned - the status the call returned
' @param expectedCode - the code the call must return and leave in error()

' Local Variables:
' @local errCode - error() as the call left it

    errCode := flash.error()
    utils.evaluateSubStatus(returned, @"status returned", expectedCode)
    utils.evaluateSubStatus(errCode, @"error() after the call", expectedCode)


PRI setTouched(firstAddr, secondAddr, thirdAddr, fourthAddr)
' Record the blocks a group touched, skipping NO_BLOCK.

' @param firstAddr - a touched block, or NO_BLOCK
' @param secondAddr - a touched block, or NO_BLOCK
' @param thirdAddr - a touched block, or NO_BLOCK
' @param fourthAddr - a touched block, or NO_BLOCK

    touchedCount := 0
    addTouched(firstAddr)
    addTouched(secondAddr)
    addTouched(thirdAddr)
    addTouched(fourthAddr)


PRI addTouched(blockAddr)
' Add a block to the touched list, unless it is NO_BLOCK or the list is full.

' @param blockAddr - a touched block, or NO_BLOCK

    if blockAddr <> NO_BLOCK and touchedCount < MAX_TOUCHED
        touchedAddr[touchedCount++] := blockAddr


PRI recordPrints(pPrints) | touchIdx
' Fingerprint every touched block into a list.

' @param pPrints - address of a list of MAX_TOUCHED longs

' Local Variables:
' @local touchIdx - number of the touched block being fingerprinted

    repeat touchedCount with touchIdx
        LONG[pPrints][touchIdx] := blockPrint(touchedAddr[touchIdx])


PRI blockPrint(blockAddr) : blockCrc | pBlock
' Fingerprint a whole block: a CRC over all its bytes.

' @param blockAddr - the block to fingerprint
' @returns blockCrc - CRC of the 4KB block, or the error code when it could not be read

' Local Variables:
' @local pBlock - address of the block read

    pBlock := flash.TEST_readBlock(blockAddr)
    if pBlock > 0
        blockCrc := getcrc(pBlock, BLOCK_CRC_POLY, flash.BLOCK_SIZE)
    else
        blockCrc := pBlock


PRI readInto(blockAddr, pDest) : pBlock
' Read a block into a buffer of the test.

' @param blockAddr - the block to read
' @param pDest - address of a buffer of flash.BLOCK_SIZE bytes, cleared when the block could not be read
' @returns pBlock - the hook's buffer address, or the error code when the block could not be read

    pBlock := flash.TEST_readBlock(blockAddr)
    if pBlock > 0
        bytemove(pDest, pBlock, flash.BLOCK_SIZE)
    else
        bytefill(pDest, 0, flash.BLOCK_SIZE)


PRI findFreeBlock(excludeAddr) : blockAddr | scanAddr, pBlock
' Find the lowest block whose lifecycle is not active, other than one block to leave out.

' @param excludeAddr - a block not to return, or NO_BLOCK
' @returns blockAddr - the block found, or NO_BLOCK when every block is active

' Local Variables:
' @local scanAddr - the block being looked at
' @local pBlock - address of that block as read

    blockAddr := NO_BLOCK
    repeat flash.BLOCKS with scanAddr
        if scanAddr <> excludeAddr
            pBlock := flash.TEST_readBlock(scanAddr)
            if pBlock > 0
                ifnot isActive(BYTE[pBlock].[CYCLE_TOP..CYCLE_BOTTOM])
                    blockAddr := scanAddr
                    quit


PRI cycleOf(pBlock) : cycle
' Give the lifecycle of a block image.

' @param pBlock - address of a block image
' @returns cycle - the lifecycle bits

    cycle := BYTE[pBlock].[CYCLE_TOP..CYCLE_BOTTOM]


PRI idOf(pBlock) : blockId
' Give the block ID of a block image.

' @param pBlock - address of a block image
' @returns blockId - the ID the block carries

    blockId := LONG[pBlock].[ID_TOP..ID_BOTTOM]


PRI nextCycle(cycle) : newerCycle
' Give the active lifecycle that is newer than an active lifecycle.

' @param cycle - an active lifecycle
' @returns newerCycle - the lifecycle a replacement of that block is given

    case cycle
        CYCLE_FIRST: newerCycle := CYCLE_SECOND
        CYCLE_SECOND: newerCycle := CYCLE_THIRD
        other: newerCycle := CYCLE_FIRST


PRI isActive(cycle) : bActive
' Tell whether a lifecycle is active: exactly one zero bit.

' @param cycle - lifecycle bits
' @returns bActive - TRUE when the lifecycle is active

    bActive := (ones cycle) == ACTIVE_ONES


PRI isCancelled(cycle) : bCancelled
' Tell whether a lifecycle is cancelled: two or three zero bits.

' @param cycle - lifecycle bits
' @returns bCancelled - TRUE when the lifecycle is cancelled

    bCancelled := (ones cycle) <= CANCELLED_MAX_ONES


PRI isCrcGood(pBlock) : bGood
' Tell whether the CRC stored at the end of a block image matches the bytes before it.

' @param pBlock - address of a block image
' @returns bGood - TRUE when the stored CRC matches

    bGood := LONG[pBlock + flash.BLOCK_SIZE - CRC_BYTES] == getcrc(pBlock, BLOCK_CRC_POLY, flash.BLOCK_SIZE - CRC_BYTES)


PRI dataMatches(pFirst, pSecond) : bSame | byteIdx
' Tell whether two block images hold the same bytes from the second byte to the CRC: everything but the lifecycle byte and the CRC.

' @param pFirst - address of a block image
' @param pSecond - address of a block image
' @returns bSame - TRUE when the bytes agree

' Local Variables:
' @local byteIdx - offset of the byte being compared

    bSame := TRUE
    repeat byteIdx from FIRST_DATA_BYTE to flash.BLOCK_SIZE - CRC_BYTES - 1
        if BYTE[pFirst][byteIdx] <> BYTE[pSecond][byteIdx]
            bSame := FALSE
            quit


PRI writeFile(pName, byteCount, seed) : bWritten | handle, writeCount, status
' Write a file of a pattern: each byte is the seed plus its offset, kept to one byte.

' @param pName - address of zstring with the file name
' @param byteCount - bytes to write
' @param seed - value of the first byte
' @returns bWritten - TRUE when every byte was written and the close succeeded

' Local Variables:
' @local handle - handle of the file
' @local writeCount - what write() returned
' @local status - what close() returned

    bWritten := FALSE
    fillPattern(byteCount, seed)
    handle := flash.open(pName, flash.FILEMODE_WRITE)
    if isUsableHandle(handle)
        writeCount := flash.write(handle, @dataBuf, byteCount)
        status := utils.closeHandle(handle)
        bWritten := writeCount == byteCount and status == flash.SUCCESS


PRI fileMatches(pName, byteCount, seed) : bMatches | handle, readCount, byteIdx
' Read a whole file and tell whether it holds the pattern writeFile() writes, and nothing more.

' @param pName - address of zstring with the file name
' @param byteCount - bytes the file must hold
' @param seed - value of its first byte
' @returns bMatches - TRUE when the size and every byte match

' Local Variables:
' @local handle - handle of the file
' @local readCount - what read() returned
' @local byteIdx - offset of the byte being compared

    bMatches := FALSE
    if flash.file_size(pName) == byteCount
        bytefill(@dataBuf, 0, byteCount)
        handle := flash.open(pName, flash.FILEMODE_READ)
        if isUsableHandle(handle)
            readCount := flash.read(handle, @dataBuf, byteCount)
            utils.closeHandle(handle)
            bMatches := readCount == byteCount
            repeat byteCount with byteIdx
                if dataBuf[byteIdx] <> (seed + byteIdx) & BYTE_MASK
                    bMatches := FALSE
                    quit


PRI fillMatches(pName, byteCount, fillValue) : bMatches | handle, readCount, chunkBytes, doneBytes, byteIdx
' Read a whole file through the data buffer, one buffer at a time, and tell whether every byte is the fill value and the size matches.

' @param pName - address of zstring with the file name
' @param byteCount - bytes the file must hold
' @param fillValue - the value every byte must hold
' @returns bMatches - TRUE when the size and every byte match

' Local Variables:
' @local handle - handle of the file
' @local readCount - what read() returned for one buffer
' @local chunkBytes - bytes asked for in one read()
' @local doneBytes - bytes read and compared so far
' @local byteIdx - offset of the byte being compared

    bMatches := FALSE
    if flash.file_size(pName) == byteCount
        handle := flash.open(pName, flash.FILEMODE_READ)
        if isUsableHandle(handle)
            bMatches := TRUE
            doneBytes := 0
            repeat while bMatches and doneBytes < byteCount
                chunkBytes := (byteCount - doneBytes) <# FILE_BYTES
                bytefill(@dataBuf, !fillValue, chunkBytes)      ' a byte read() did not write cannot match
                readCount := flash.read(handle, @dataBuf, chunkBytes)
                bMatches := readCount == chunkBytes
                repeat chunkBytes with byteIdx
                    if dataBuf[byteIdx] <> fillValue
                        bMatches := FALSE
                        quit
                doneBytes += chunkBytes
            utils.closeHandle(handle)


PRI fillPattern(byteCount, seed) | byteIdx
' Fill the data buffer with the pattern: each byte is the seed plus its offset, kept to one byte.

' @param byteCount - bytes to fill
' @param seed - value of the first byte

' Local Variables:
' @local byteIdx - offset of the byte being filled

    repeat byteCount with byteIdx
        dataBuf[byteIdx] := (seed + byteIdx) & BYTE_MASK


PRI isUsableHandle(handle) : bUsable
' Tell whether a value is one of the handles open() hands out.

' @param handle - value open() returned
' @returns bUsable - TRUE when the value is inside the range of handles

    bUsable := handle >= utils.FIRST_HANDLE and handle < utils.FIRST_HANDLE + flash.MAX_FILES_OPEN


